==Important events==
{{spoilers}}
* {{adv|Cheren}} is revealed to have become a teacher at the [[Aspertia City]]'s [[Aspertia Gym|Trainers' School]].
* {{adv|Whitley}} transfers into the Trainers' School.
* {{adv|Blake}} and Whitley receive [[Pokédex]]es.
* Whitley is revealed to be a former member of [[Team Plasma]].
* Blake is revealed to be a member of the [[International Police]].
* [[Drayden]] calls Cheren to inform him about {{p|Kyurem}}.
* {{TP|Blake|Genesect}} appears and is revealed to be Team Plasma's secret weapon developed at the [[P2 Laboratory]].
* [[Colress]] is revealed to be behind {{p|Genesect}}'s development and to be Team Plasma's new leader.
* Genesect is revealed to be controlled by a machine instead of being a caught Pokémon. Blake successfully captures the Pokémon.
* It is revealed that there was schism within Team Plasma and important research data was entrusted to a {{adv|Whitley|young girl}}.
* Blake tries to get closer to Whitley and takes her to [[Pledge Grove]] where they are attacked by {{p|Keldeo}}.
* Cheren takes the class on a trip to [[Pokéstar Studios]], and Whitley and Blake participate in a movie.
* [[Brycen]] is revealed to have quit his job as a [[Gym Leader]] and suggests that Cheren become Aspertia City's Gym Leader.
* {{adv|White}} is revealed to have had a part in Pokéstar Studios's creation.
* Hugh finds Whitley's pendant, which contains a microchip inside.
* Hugh discovers data containing information on Pokémon liberated by Team Plasma on the microchip, vowing to find her.
* Hugh flashes back to five years ago, where the {{p|Purrloin}} he gave to his [[Hugh's sister|sister]] for her birthday was stolen by Team Plasma.

